<title>FRANCE: Seafrance adds fourth ship on Calais-Dover line.</title>
<headline>Seafrance adds fourth ship on Calais-Dover line.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-12-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>French shipping company Seafrance said on Tuesday that it added a fourth ship to the Calais-Dover route to satisfy a rise in demand since a fire in the Channel Tunnel on November 18 disrupted Eurotunnel's freight service.</p>
<p>Seafrance said the &quot;Seafrance Nord Pas de Calais&quot;, introduced last Friday, would be dedicated to freight service and conduct three to five round trips daily.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom, +33 1 4221 5452</p>
